A||||13||Fret Naught||What is it?||||5||
Z||000000||Fret Naught||06-03-2000||02:22 PM||||Dumb question guys,<BR>what the heck is that little LED located on my center console top center? Some kind of alarm system? if it is, it is disabled and I would like to repair and enable it.<P>Off topic, I am going to purchase a digital camera, (so I can post pics easier) any suggestions? I don't want to spend more than 300.00<BR>Thanks in advance||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||06-03-2000||02:37 PM||||Don't know without a pic. but if it is a <BR>alarm system of some kind, it is a after market system. You will need to locate<BR>the rest of the unit and hunt down some <BR>wires.  Also I have seen the "fake" ones<BR>that are just a LED/blinking light????<P>Here is a pic of my alarm LED the little red dot next to the air vent on the left.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=21451561&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=21451561&Sequence=2</A> <P>Hope this helps<BR>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 06-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-03-2000||02:38 PM||||The LED most likely goes to an alarm system. If the brain box for the alarm is still in the car it will most likely be under the driverside dash. You should be able to follow thw wires from the LED right to it.<BR>As for camera's I have an HP C200 that takes<BR>80 low res, 40 hi res and 17 super hi res pics. It has 2 zoom levels and it was only $289 at Circuit City. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick's Dad||06-03-2000||08:09 PM||||Hi Fret,<P>Try the Olympus D-360 for a camera. It doesn't have an optical zoom, but it can do closeups within a few inches; perfect for taking pictures of LED's (Of which my Formula, save for the radio, has none. I suspect, as well, that it is alarm related). If you want to see a pic, try <A HREF="http://www.cameraco.com/onlinestore/detail.asp?productid=429" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cameraco.com/onlinestore/detail.asp?productid=429</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||06-03-2000||09:04 PM||||I agree about the LED.. most likely from an alarm. <P>Unless the previous owner had installed some sort of jet afterburner system, and the light blinks when you hit mach 1... Or maybe he was a superhero.. and light blinks when he had to change into a costume and become FieroMan, and save the world from the dreaded RiceBoy...... <BR>Hey, ya never know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>anyway, I'd also like to get a digital camera.. My favorite is the Mavica. having it save the pics directly to floppy is very nice. I can't afford one though. anyone know of a fairly cheap camera that takes at least 1024 x 768 res. (max.. 640 x 480 would be low quality) photos, has an LCD screen for previewing the pics..... and connects to the computer via USB?<P>thanks!||||reg||10
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||06-03-2000||09:20 PM||||DaRkLoRD what is the price of the camera that puts the pics right on a disk?<P>FieroMan..........Huuuuuuum save the world from Rice Boy. Where did you get that? Is it on TV, comic book, (lol)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> That is funny <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BN Boomer||06-03-2000||10:21 PM||||I bought a Sony Mavica FD-88 for $699 a couple of months ago. Being able save pictures directly to a floppy disk is really convenient, in my opinion. Sony has less expensive models that can be found for less than $500 on the internet and Panasonic has a camera that records ro floppy disks, too. C-net.com is a great place to look for anything computer related.||||reg||1
